  "worked_solution": "First, we have to find $p+q.$ According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $p+q$ goes from the tail of $p$ to the head of $q:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251721/assets/68c14ce5ff66272986e958f09f30289d56519e90b34fae23362753f84c042a50.png)\n\nIn $△AHB$, we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=2$ and $BH=3.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|p+q| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $p+q$ is $\\sqrt{13}.$ Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{|p+q|}\\cdot (p+q) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}(p+q).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
